{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice","id":128551,"title":"Help choose Auspice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-08T15:15:46-07:00","id":128551,"title":"Help choose Auspice","content":"So I start my <b>Werewolf</b> game, centered in small town in the middle of Swedish <i>Scandes</i> mountains, locked in the valley full of snow. As game starts with characters being before FIrst Change, crutial is to make appropiate Auspices calls on characters. One of players is more versed in <b>Forsaken</b> and he said he want's his PC to be <i>Rahu</i>, so it's one chosen. Rest of players are new to setting and I would rather myself choose them and make First Change in good time.<br /> <br /> So here is first character to help decied about Auspice...<br /> <br /> <i><b>Manfred</b> is middle acclaimed resercher in studeid in both academic and science subjects. He is taking year of sabbatical from his career as he feel a bit burn out by his work. But there are also rumors about his controversial reaserch funding. He moves to town about month ago, but he shun people. He isn't totally closed on others, just thinks that books and long mountin hicking are better than most people.</i><br /> <br /> So what Auspice would you put to this character? I was thinking mostly on Elodoth or Ithaeur, but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-09-2014, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:20:33-07:00","id":128553,"title":"","content":"It depends on if you want Luna to build on what he's like or has something else in mind. As he stands he's a lot like an Ithauer or an Irraka, but Luna might not care and burn the Cahalunim's or Rahlunim's mark into him.<br /> <br /> If I had to pick one, I'd go Ithauer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:27:22-07:00","id":128558,"title":"","content":"I know player a lot, and he always play calm and steady characters. He even complains he sometimes is &quot;outside&quot; his character he plays, and looks on everything from diffrent possition, like a spectator in the theater. Looking on this, I'm myself more inclined for making <b>Manfred</b> in to Ithauer, but would gladly hear what you have on his other options to Change and reasoning on them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T17:04:53-07:00","id":128625,"title":"","content":"Go with what ever you think the player would enjoy the most. No need for his character's personality to enter into the equation. Plenty of calm, rational people go through their first change at the full moon, plenty of dim witted and boisterous people first change at the new moon, etc. Luna works in mysterious ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T21:16:02-07:00","id":128727,"title":"","content":"Roll a D6:<br /> <br /> 1: Irraka;<br /> 2: Ithaeur;<br /> 3: Elodoth;<br /> 4: Cahalith;<br /> 5: Rahu;<br /> 6: Roll again.<br /> <br /> That's how Luna does it, I heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T22:29:06-07:00","id":128760,"title":"","content":"Take Charlaquin's advice. Explain the auspices and have the player pick - players usually like it when they get to play characters that fit their play style.<br /> <br /> If he absolutely refuses to pick, take Ephsy's advice and have the Moon decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T01:10:22-07:00","id":128810,"title":"","content":"Explaining Auspices to players is bad idea when you want to make it really mysterious Change for new players, first time playing WoD. They don't know what's happening in game and in character, so they are more attuned to it, and <i>feel</i> it better. In <b>Mage</b> I ask players to choose two Arcana, with one more important - no talks about Paths, no details powers, just most basic info that is not needed in descision. And best, in my opinion, would be if players needed to choose - but with mages is imposible. Mostly in <b>Werewolf</b> I can guess what would work for PCs as Auspice, but there are sometimes debatable characters and I was wanting to see how other STs decide on them. From what I see you just roll dice to see what players should have, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-09-2014, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T02:20:06-07:00","id":128835,"title":"","content":"Just ask what archetype they want to play, or what they think their character most represents - assassin, thief, shaman, judge, face, storyteller, lore keeper, warrior etc. Then assign auspice based on that decision. Easy, and players don't feel robbed by your choice on their behalf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T09:29:53-07:00","id":129023,"title":"","content":"You should rather go with Archetypes defined in Lore of the Forsaken, they're less obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T09:51:53-07:00","id":129047,"title":"","content":"If you want a mysterious change, just roll for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T09:52:20-07:00","id":129048,"title":"","content":"There are so many archetypes that can fit the Auspices, it would be easy to find one that fits some aspect of each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T10:14:03-07:00","id":129061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=129048#post129048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are so many archetypes that can fit the Auspices, it would be easy to find one that fits some aspect of each.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get this. But I think for starting players going for sterotypical Auspice isn't bad thing. It's like in D&amp;D you don't give new players advanced Classes, only give them basic ones.<br /> <br /> Talked a bit with player in question and he goes for &quot;lore-keeper&quot; archetype. So I think <i>Ithaeur</i> is in order for <b>Manfred</b> PC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T10:36:22-07:00","id":129081,"title":"","content":"Lore-Keepers are Cahaliths, ironically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T10:56:44-07:00","id":129098,"title":"","content":"What? From new Auspices spoiler I get idea that <i>Cathaliths</i> are more active in <b>Idigam Chronicles</b>, being more Bard/Fae-like figure. And that <i>Ithaeur </i>is about gathering and keeping knowlegde of the pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Idigam Chronicles Auspices spoiler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><b>Irraka</b> hunt their prey without being seen, striking from the shadows. In a pack, the Irraka makes sure that the kill happens, even if she doesn\u2019t strike the final blow \u2014 hamstringing her prey, or leaving them open to another werewolf\u2019s claws. On her own, she remains hidden and builds every advantage she can find, then goes for the kill in a single moment of blinding violence.</li> <li><b>Ithaeur</b> know that they are never alone. His knowledge and connections in the spirit world have obvious utility in the <i>hisil.</i> When hunting in the material world, those spirits give him a thousand ephemeral eyes eyes to track his prey, a thousand hands that reach out to Urge or Claim for just a moment before the werewolf\u2019s teeth sink in.</li> <li><b>Elodoth</b> have one foot in light and one in shadow. As such, they foster connections in both worlds. She makes deals with anything, from spirits of rock and toxic waste to the cops who watch the corner. She sits in the middle of a network of connections and favors, pulling on \u2014 or breaking \u2014 strings that make her prey\u2019s life hell before he even knows the werewolf is after him.</li> <li><b>Cahalith</b> have a blessing from Luna. The moon comes to their dreams and gives visions of the hunt. As such, a Cahalith knows the story of the hunt before it starts, and it\u2019s then his role to make the hunt memorable. As such, he leaves subtlety to other packmates. The Cahalith howls so his prey can hear, bursts through walls, and leaves his prey in no doubt of what is coming for her.</li> <li><b>Rahu</b> are the blade of the guillotine. Other werewolves prime the hunt, weaken and harry their prey, but it\u2019s the Rahu who kills the prey. Sometimes, it\u2019s an execution. Sometimes, it\u2019s a drawn-out fight. Many Rahu prefer the fight. The full moon casts many things into light and shadow. The fight \u2014 the kill \u2014 is her role in the hunt. That\u2019s all a Rahu needs to know.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-09-2014, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T11:24:04-07:00","id":129112,"title":"","content":"In the specific write up for Cahaltih, it points out blatantly that the Cahalith retain their role as lore keepers.<br /> <br /> Which still makes sense-if you wanna make a good story of something, it helps if you have a store of good(and sometimes bad) stories to inspire you. Such stories have lots of uses asides from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T11:45:16-07:00","id":129141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=129112#post129112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which still makes sense-if you wanna make a good story of something, it helps if you have a store of good(and sometimes bad) stories to inspire you. Such stories have lots of uses asides from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stories, not lore. Stories are legends about previous accomplishments of Uratha ancestors. Lore is knowlegde what are spirits Ban, how to bargin with Spirits Court, what is problem with Pure attacking in previous years. Stories are vision, lore is facts and usefullness,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T12:08:42-07:00","id":129160,"title":"","content":"With the Uratha's ample oral tradition... where do you think they get their Lore from? How do you think they teach newly changed? With stories. It's the most ancient form of Lore there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T12:25:46-07:00","id":129176,"title":"","content":"Stories and lore are pretty much one and the same in my mind. The only real distinction is that plain old lore tends to be a little bit boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T12:41:03-07:00","id":129187,"title":"","content":"The Cahalith keeps stories of werewolves; the Ithaeur keeps stories of spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T12:50:17-07:00","id":129192,"title":"","content":"That's a little simplistic-remember, Cahalith do serve in the Bone Shadows and the Iron Masters, and asides from that stories about spirits can appeal to anyone.<br /> <br /> The big difference is that the Cahalith keep stories, the Ithaeur keep instruction manuals. One might resemble the other, but the Ithaeur ultimately are more interested in the mechanics of spirits and the Cahalith are more interested in the fluff. The two aren't inseparable, and both are useful to the other, but the divide still begins there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-09-2014, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T13:15:47-07:00","id":129213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=129187#post129187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cahalith keeps stories of werewolves; the Ithaeur keeps stories of spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Some Ithaeur might recognize the wisdom in listening to the stories of their preferred prey (spirits, I'm not talking about a tribal sacred prey here). Cahalith are expected, in one fashion or another, to keep every relevant tidbit of lore pertaining their territory, physical or spiritual. It's one of it's aspects. Be it stored in spreadsheets of numerical facts, or their own journals with encyclopedic entries written in First Tongue glyphs.<br /> <br /> Just like the Rahu could be a mindless berserker or a tactician.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T13:22:19-07:00","id":129222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=129192#post129192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big difference is that the Cahalith keep stories, the Ithaeur keep instruction manuals. One might resemble the other, but the Ithaeur ultimately are more interested in the mechanics of spirits and the Cahalith are more interested in the fluff. The two aren't inseparable, and both are useful to the other, but the divide still begins there.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are same pointing to <i>Ithaeur</i>, looking on character concept...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice#post128551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Manfred</b> is middle acclaimed resercher in studeid in both academic and science subjects. He is taking year of sabbatical from his career as he feel a bit burn out by his work. But there are also rumors about his controversial reaserch funding. He moves to town about month ago, but he shun people. He isn't totally closed on others, just thinks that books and long mountin hicking are better than most people.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>He is dedicated in to studies knowlegde, being scientist, from the concept look. And at least books are agreeing with me - <b>Lore of Forsaken</b> have this Archetypes for <i>Ithaeur</i>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> GREAT MEMORY<br /> All Ithaeur have a natural af\ufb01nity for learning. Some have a drive for it that becomes almost their reason for being. It may have started in childhood, as the young <i>nuzusul</i> devoured everything she could get her hands on, only to be awakened in a wash of horror and pain by a moon that told her there was even more to learn. Or it might have come on like a hurricane wind after the Change \u2014 the feeling that every minute of human life had been a waste, that there are no longer enough nights left to learn everything about the real world. A Great Memory may be powerfully intelligent, or of average intelligence but have great conviction. Great <br /> Memories tend to accumulate as much knowledge as they can, and may even have eidetic memory. A Great Memory makes a \ufb01erce and careful hunter of spirits: there is no way to drive her away when you can \ufb01nd out something new. She hounds the spirits of knowledge and memory whenever she can \ufb01nd them; they are not friends, but they can be bribed and forced into teaching her lore. </div> </div> </div>And second one also looks like it could be great fit for character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> SCIENTIST<br /> Some Ithaeur don\u2019t approach their tasks with the reverence of the devout. The Scientist may not have any particular scienti\ufb01c training, but he has the mindset of <br /> a human researcher \u2014 he wants to understand why rites work, why spirits behave the way they do, how best to use this knowledge for the bene\ufb01t of the pack. The Scientist maps the symbolism of the spirit world with the intent of mapping the sympathetic connections. Some Ithaeur with this archetype may be skeptics who are actively searching for holes in the legend of Father Wolf and Mother Luna \u2014 and such holes do exist \u2014 but others simply want to learn and understand. The most brilliant and innovative of the Scientists are those who take nothing for granted, who are interested in learning the ways of the Shadow whether they particularly like the answers or not. </div> </div> </div>For <b>Manfred</b> I will stick wih <i>Ithaeur</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T13:36:32-07:00","id":129232,"title":"","content":"Well, again, that's useful in a limited way. Luna is fucking insane, and she might well decide that guy is Rahu material.<br /> <br /> Depends on how mysterious you want it to be, I guess. but persona wise, yes, I like the character as an Ithaeur.<br /> <br /> (I played a character once I had all decked out to be a Rahu, and the Gm decided to make him an Ithaeur. I had a lot of fun working with and around that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T13:50:02-07:00","id":129237,"title":"","content":"Second player made interesting combination when shown archetypes from <b>Bunyip</b> idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=128835#post128835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just ask what archetype they want to play, or what they think their character most represents - assassin, thief, shaman, judge, face, storyteller, lore keeper, warrior etc. Then assign auspice based on that decision. Easy, and players don't feel robbed by your choice on their behalf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Player made young bisnessman that wants to assess town posibilites as new regions market. And then he chosen Assassin as his future. Very intersitng <i>Irraka</i> can come of it I must say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-10-2014, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T13:59:57-07:00","id":129242,"title":"","content":"I can't hear the name &quot;Manfred&quot; without thinking of &quot;Monster of the Sky&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/samkoji/monster-of-the-sky-a-mythic-tale-of-love-and-reven\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...love-and-reven</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>I am the rider of the wind<br /> The stirrer of the storm<br /> A hurricane of rage<br /> In human form<br /> And now the hour has arrived<br /> And this vow I renew<br /> I am a monster of the sky<br /> And I\u2019m coming after you</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#121A0D\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- &quot;Monster of the Sky&quot; lyrics by Stereo Alchemy (inspired by Lord Byron)</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T18:56:34-07:00","id":129493,"title":"","content":"Cahalith, Elodoth, and Ithaeur have always had a bit of overlap. Lore-keepers, truth-seekers, and shamans sort of have intrinsically interconnected roles in the large scheme of things. The way I've always sort of internalized it is something along the lines of the Truth-Seeker discovers what is true, the Shaman dissects it for hidden meanings and purpose, the Lore-Keeper weaves it into a story that it can arrange with others into a narrative. I've found it very hard to make a single werewolf character who can mechanically do all three, they each get something exclusive in one way or another that helps but doesn't cover all the bases.<br /> <br /> In short you go to an Ithaeur for a textbook, you go to a Cahalith for a novel.<br /> <br /> That said I've generally found that there are a number of ways to work with a character's auspice. It can be a straight forward arrangement, the warrior guy gets the warrior auspice and is like &quot;Okay, cool.&quot; It can be somewhat confusing, with the warrior guy getting the Scout's sign for instance...did Luna make a mistake or is she trying to tell you something? Do you embrace it or rebel against it? In your rebellion do you discover that it truly is your calling? If you embrace it, does it just never quite click into place? None of these are inherently bad stories to be told.<br /> <br /> That being said I wouldn't be comfortable making such a big character decision for a player. I would let the player decide what they want out of their character's auspice, maybe make some suggestions, and run with it in the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T19:28:05-07:00","id":129522,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, the distinction between Cahalith and Ithaeur seems best represented as a diversity of cause versus effect. A Cahalith understands the multitude of ways a given story can be read based on time and tenor, with the effect on the listener varying accordingly. An Ithaeur understands the ways to make a given thing happen, whether by Gift or rite or spiritual favor or mundane solution.<br /> <br /> A Gibbous Moon tells a ghost story around a campfire to spook the mortals in preparation for a Hunt, and can spin that same story in a different context to make his pack weep for the dead. He has a versatile cause with widely varying strengths of effect.<br /> <br /> A Crescent Moon uses the Rite of Chosen Ground to evoke a resonance of fear in her lands to make the campers afraid, but calls in a favor from a minor spirit of grief she defeated in a test of endurance to lend the right aura of mourning to the funeral. She knows a number of different causes to use to generate a desired effect.<br /> <br /> <i>Why?</i> versus <i>How?</i> may be a more succinct way of phrasing it, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T15:58:26-07:00","id":139909,"title":"","content":"So I have a new player and character to the play - <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Huntsman, don't like to be alone, so he often goes to bar, or he talks to animals and he thinks they talks him back. He likes to work alone, but goes either way. </div> </div> </div>Quick test with Auspices archetypes marked his as either Cathalith or Elodoth. Groups lacks both, but to me character ( and probably a player ) would more like the Cathalith. Is there any things to take in consideration for choosing Elodoth over Cathalith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T16:34:11-07:00","id":139947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=139909#post139909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have a new player and character to the play -<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Quick test with Auspices archetypes marked his as either Cathalith or Elodoth. Groups lacks both, but to me character ( and probably a player ) would more like the Cathalith. Is there any things to take in consideration for choosing Elodoth over Cathalith?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you are looking at this whole thing slightly incomplete. My reasoning is that Tribe also plays a significant factor for characters and personality. Auspice is the role that Luna chooses for them, while Tribe is for likeminded individuals (more or less). Your latest character I could see being an Irraka for Auspice, but an Iron Master for Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T22:12:13-07:00","id":140262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=139947#post139947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your latest character I could see being an Irraka for Auspice, but an Iron Master for Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ekhem, Irraka that don't want to be alone and talks much to other people and animals? Is it only me the <i>Cathalith</i> is best take on this, while <i>Elodoth</i> is always second better?<br /> <br /> And how Iron Masters come to mind as Tribe? From that he drinks in bar often? So that 50% of werewolf population should be Iron Masters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Don't get me wrong, Iron Masters are my private favorites, especially now as they HUNT HUMANS! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-17-2014, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T00:58:21-07:00","id":140323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=139909#post139909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Huntsman, don't like to be alone, so he often goes to bar, or he talks to animals and he thinks they talks him back. He likes to work alone, but goes either way. </i><br /> <br /> Quick test with Auspices archetypes marked his as either Cathalith or Elodoth. Groups lacks both, but to me character ( and probably a player ) would more like the Cathalith. Is there any things to take in consideration for choosing Elodoth over Cathalith?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ithaeur. He likes to go out alone but not really be alone? That has spirit master written all over it. Going away from his pack but talking with what he finds all around him is Ithaeur.<br /> <br /> He's not Elodoth - he doesn't care anything for balance or settling disputes. He's not Cahalith - he doesn't want to be among the crowd, regaling them with stories of prowess and encouraging others to be bigger and better.<br /> <br /> Ithaeur.<br /> <br /> *Caveat - this is based solely on the one line description and doesn't intend to capture any other depth the character may have.<br /> <br /> As for tribe? Anything but Storm Lords. He doesn't like to be alone so he hangs out in bars? He's showing his weakness and letting others tend to it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T01:46:09-07:00","id":140339,"title":"","content":"<b>Bunyip</b>, thanks for advice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=140323#post140323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ithaeur. He likes to go out alone but not really be alone? That has spirit master written all over it. Going away from his pack but talking with what he finds all around him is Ithaeur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting interpretation. But we have one <i>Ithaeur</i> ( <b>Manfred</b> character from before ) and I'm more inclined with &quot;storyteller&quot; idea. I made player your achetype test and he answered that he would want him to become &quot;face storyteller&quot;, so player is more for <i>Elodoth</i>-<i>Cahalith</i> option I spose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=140323#post140323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's not Elodoth - he doesn't care anything for balance or settling disputes. He's not Cahalith - he doesn't want to be among the crowd, regaling them with stories of prowess and encouraging others to be bigger and better.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Elodoth</i> maybe not. But I could imagine quiet, serial-killer like <i>Cathalith</i> that gloated of his and packs horrible stories in times of rest and preparing for next hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/128551-help-choose-auspice?p=140323#post140323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for tribe? Anything but Storm Lords. He doesn't like to be alone so he hangs out in bars? He's showing his weakness and letting others tend to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I at least not make him <i>Storm Lord</i>. Players will choose later in game, but probably I would propose him <i>Hunters in Darkness</i> - good Tribe for huntsman character, and letting purity in the life is somehow coherent with basic concept. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T14:08:44-07:00","id":152957,"title":"","content":"So we have fifth, last character to our game - young, sociology quail who is returning to her home town to help her parents, but her childhood friend is dead and she wants to dwell deep in to this case after few days from funeral. I think to make her parents as part of cult of Malejin. She will have Virtue of <i>Honest</i> and Vice as <i>Inappropriate.</i><br /> <br /> I really thinks she could work as<i> Elodoth</i>. She &quot;illuminates the case&quot; of dead friend, what to be honest in her ways and making inappropriate moves. It sounds to me like &quot;lawful&quot; and &quot;judge&quot;, I think the archetype the Elodoth represent. She also wants to balance things, in spiritual sense.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}